Plan for workload pg-main: Planned, site b to site a
Ledger: SiteFailover tack-system/pg-main-20261027-101500 at site a

Sites:
  a  Replica  declares b  healthy  Cluster db/pg-a: phase "Cluster in healthy state", declares pg-b primary, pod pg-a-1, timeline 1; Pooler pg-a-rw has 0 instances
  b  Primary  declares b  healthy  Cluster db/pg-b: phase "Cluster in healthy state", declares pg-b primary, pod pg-b-1, timeline 1; Pooler pg-b-rw has 2 instances

Hold
   1. hold-a-cluster-pg-a  site a
      hold Cluster db/pg-a at site a: Flux stops applying it
        annotate Cluster db/pg-a: kustomize.toolkit.fluxcd.io/reconcile=disabled, failover.tako.id/held-by=pg-main-20261027-101500
        applied by Flux Kustomization flux-system/a
   2. hold-a-pooler-pg-a-rw  site a
      hold Pooler db/pg-a-rw at site a: Flux stops applying it
        annotate Pooler db/pg-a-rw: kustomize.toolkit.fluxcd.io/reconcile=disabled, failover.tako.id/held-by=pg-main-20261027-101500
        applied by Flux Kustomization flux-system/a
   3. reconcile-hold-a  site a
      reconcile Flux at site a, so no apply started before the hold is still in flight
        request a reconcile of Kustomizations flux-system/a and their GitRepository; wait up to 5m0s
   4. hold-b-cluster-pg-b  site b
      hold Cluster db/pg-b at site b: Flux stops applying it
        annotate Cluster db/pg-b: kustomize.toolkit.fluxcd.io/reconcile=disabled, failover.tako.id/held-by=pg-main-20261027-101500
        applied by Flux Kustomization flux-system/b
   5. hold-b-pooler-pg-b-rw  site b
      hold Pooler db/pg-b-rw at site b: Flux stops applying it
        annotate Pooler db/pg-b-rw: kustomize.toolkit.fluxcd.io/reconcile=disabled, failover.tako.id/held-by=pg-main-20261027-101500
        applied by Flux Kustomization flux-system/b
   6. reconcile-hold-b  site b
      reconcile Flux at site b, so no apply started before the hold is still in flight
        request a reconcile of Kustomizations flux-system/b and their GitRepository; wait up to 5m0s
Failover
   7. pooler-b  site b
      set Pooler pg-b-rw to 0 instances
        patch Pooler db/pg-b-rw (merge): {"spec":{"instances":0}}
   8. wait-pooler-b  site b
      wait until the Pooler pg-b-rw runs no pod
        wait up to 10m0s on Deployment db/pg-b-rw until:
          {.status.replicas} is empty
   9. demote-b  site b
      demote Cluster pg-b: declare pg-a primary and drop any old token
        patch Cluster db/pg-b (merge): {"spec":{"replica":{"primary":"pg-a","promotionToken":null}}}
  10. wait-demoted-b  site b
      wait until Cluster pg-b has demoted and published its demotion token
        wait up to 10m0s on Cluster db/pg-b until:
          {.status.demotionToken} is not empty
          {.status.switchReplicaClusterStatus.inProgress} NotEquals "true"
  11. capture-token  site b
      record the demotion token of Cluster pg-b in the ledger
        record {.status.demotionToken} of Cluster db/pg-b in the ledger as $(demotionToken)
  12. promote-a  site a
      promote Cluster pg-a with the demotion token, in one patch
        patch Cluster db/pg-a (merge): {"spec":{"replica":{"primary":"pg-a","promotionToken":"$(demotionToken)"}}}
  13. wait-promoted-a  site a
      wait until Cluster pg-a has used the token and runs a healthy primary
        wait up to 10m0s on Cluster db/pg-a until:
          {.status.lastPromotionToken} Equals "$(demotionToken)"
          {.status.instancesReportedState.*.isPrimary} Contains "true"
          {.status.phase} Equals "Cluster in healthy state"
  14. clear-token-a  site a
      remove the used token from Cluster pg-a, so it can never apply again
        patch Cluster db/pg-a (merge): {"spec":{"replica":{"promotionToken":null}}}
  15. pooler-a  site a
      set Pooler pg-a-rw to 2 instances
        patch Pooler db/pg-a-rw (merge): {"spec":{"instances":2}}
  16. wait-pooler-a  site a
      wait until the Pooler pg-a-rw has 2 ready pods
        wait up to 10m0s on Deployment db/pg-a-rw until:
          {.status.readyReplicas} Equals "2"
  17. verify-a  site a
      verify that Cluster pg-a is a healthy primary and declares itself
        wait up to 10m0s on Cluster db/pg-a until:
          {.spec.replica.primary} Equals "pg-a"
          {.status.instancesReportedState.*.isPrimary} Contains "true"
          {.status.phase} Equals "Cluster in healthy state"
PromoteToGitOps
  18. git-commit  Git
      commit the live state to https://git.example.com/gitops.git branch main
        clusters/a/cluster.yaml: spec.replica.primary = "pg-a"  (site a, Cluster db/pg-a spec.replica.primary)
        clusters/a/cluster.yaml: spec.replica.promotionToken removed  (site a, Cluster db/pg-a spec.replica.promotionToken)
        clusters/a/pooler.yaml: spec.instances = 2  (site a, Pooler db/pg-a-rw spec.instances)
        clusters/b/cluster.yaml: spec.replica.primary = "pg-a"  (site b, Cluster db/pg-b spec.replica.primary)
        clusters/b/cluster.yaml: spec.replica.promotionToken removed  (site b, Cluster db/pg-b spec.replica.promotionToken)
        clusters/b/pooler.yaml: spec.instances = 0  (site b, Pooler db/pg-b-rw spec.instances)
        commit message: tack: pg-main primary b to a (planned)
  19. reconcile-git-a  site a
      wait for Flux at site a to apply the run's commit (held objects stay as they are)
        request a reconcile of Kustomizations flux-system/a and their GitRepository; wait up to 5m0s
        until Flux has applied $(git.commit)
  20. reconcile-git-b  site b
      wait for Flux at site b to apply the run's commit (held objects stay as they are)
        request a reconcile of Kustomizations flux-system/b and their GitRepository; wait up to 5m0s
        until Flux has applied $(git.commit)
Release
  21. verify-git-a  site a
      check at site a that Git, as Flux renders it, equals live
        render the run's commit as Flux would and diff it against 2 live objects; stop if they differ
  22. release-a-cluster-pg-a  site a
      release Cluster db/pg-a at site a: Flux applies it again
        remove from Cluster db/pg-a: kustomize.toolkit.fluxcd.io/reconcile, failover.tako.id/held-by
  23. release-a-pooler-pg-a-rw  site a
      release Pooler db/pg-a-rw at site a: Flux applies it again
        remove from Pooler db/pg-a-rw: kustomize.toolkit.fluxcd.io/reconcile, failover.tako.id/held-by
  24. reconcile-release-a  site a
      reconcile Flux at site a with the released objects
        request a reconcile of Kustomizations flux-system/a and their GitRepository; wait up to 5m0s
        until Flux has applied $(git.commit)
  25. verify-noop-a  site a
      check at site a that Flux changed nothing
        check that the generation of 2 released objects did not change
  26. verify-git-b  site b
      check at site b that Git, as Flux renders it, equals live
        render the run's commit as Flux would and diff it against 2 live objects; stop if they differ
  27. release-b-cluster-pg-b  site b
      release Cluster db/pg-b at site b: Flux applies it again
        remove from Cluster db/pg-b: kustomize.toolkit.fluxcd.io/reconcile, failover.tako.id/held-by
  28. release-b-pooler-pg-b-rw  site b
      release Pooler db/pg-b-rw at site b: Flux applies it again
        remove from Pooler db/pg-b-rw: kustomize.toolkit.fluxcd.io/reconcile, failover.tako.id/held-by
  29. reconcile-release-b  site b
      reconcile Flux at site b with the released objects
        request a reconcile of Kustomizations flux-system/b and their GitRepository; wait up to 5m0s
        until Flux has applied $(git.commit)
  30. verify-noop-b  site b
      check at site b that Flux changed nothing
        check that the generation of 2 released objects did not change

Nothing was changed. To run this plan: tack run -f testdata/workload.yaml --to a --from b --mode planned
